  {
    "id": "c061",
    "name": "Section 10.4—No Representations or Results Warranty",
    "text": "4, Licensor makes absolutely no representations regarding the suitability, character, effectiveness, legitimacy, legality, trust worthiness, non-infringing nature, or usefulness of the System(s) herein licensed and Licensee uses this License knowing no such representations of any nature regarding same have been made, Without limiting the aforesaid, Licensor makes no agreement, warranty, guaranty, assurance or affirmation that Licensee or Licensee’s clients will achieve any particular result from the use of the System(s) herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c062",
    "name": "Section 10.5—Licensee Indemnification",
    "text": "5, Licensee will indemnify, defend and hold harmless ARP and ARP’S agents, officers, employees, directors, volunteers and authorized representatives from any and all losses, liabilities, charges, damages, claims, liens, causes of action, awards, judgments, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees and costs of litigation) by any third party resulting from any acts or omissions of Licensee relating to its activities in connection with this Agreement, Licensee's breach of this Agreement, or Licensee's misrepresentations relating to ARP, the Systems or this Agreement, regardless of the form of action. Licensee will be solely responsible for any claims, warranties or representations made by Licensee or Licensee's representatives or agents which differ from the warranties provided by ARP herein or in the applicable end user license agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c063",
    "name": "Section 10.6—Notice and Defense of Claims",
    "text": "6. ARP shall give the Licensee reasonable notice of any claim or litigation as to which the Licensee has an indemnification obligation hereunder. The Licensee shall, at its sole expense, assume the defense thereof, and ARP shall provide the Licensee with reasonable cooperation in such defense. If ARP desires to appoint counsel to participate in such defense, in addition to counsel supplied by the Licensee, it may do so at tts own expense, but the Licensee and counsel provided by the Licensee shall have the right to control said defense."
